If the math adds up then one knows they have enough descriptors. Descriptors are important for the math. It does not mean Exception Theory's math is wrong, it needs to be checked to ensure all proper descriptors are applied. Descriptors bridge indeterminacy and points, it is the only thing that can really get close to them. Just like how in another way, indeterminacy is the agency that bridges the infinite and the finite. Descriptors can never truly reach them, but it can come close. There is no infinite precision, as it must be thus.